@title Reading Your Quarterly Water Bill
@subtitle A guide from Tarn Valley Water

kpi Billing period | 3 months | every quarter
kpi Payment due | 21 days | after the issue date
kpi Autopay saving | $2 | off each bill | good

## Your bill at a glance
Each bill has three parts: the water you used, a sewer charge and a fixed service charge. For example, a household that used 72 m3 in a quarter would see this bill:

table = Item,Amount; "Usage, first 30 m3 at $1.85",$55.50; "Usage, next 30 m3 at $2.60",$78.00; "Usage, last 12 m3 at $3.90",$46.80; "Usage total, 72 m3",$180.30; "Sewer charge, 80% of usage",$144.24; Fixed service charge,$38.40; **Total bill**,**$362.94**

## Usage charges
Water is metered in cubic meters (m3) and charged in three tiers:
- The first 30 m3 cost $1.85 per m3.
- The next 30 m3 cost $2.60 per m3.
- Anything above 60 m3 costs $3.90 per m3.

## Fixed charges
The sewer charge is 80% of your usage charge. The fixed service charge is $38.40 per quarter.

## Ways to pay
Payment is due 21 days after the issue date. You can pay:
- Online at [tarnvalleywater.example/pay](https://tarnvalleywater.example/pay)
- By phone on 555-0121
- In person at the Main Street office on weekdays from 8:30 to 16:30

If you sign up for autopay, $2 comes off each bill.

## If you cannot pay on time
If you cannot pay, call 555-0133 before the due date to set up a payment plan. A late fee of 5% is added after 30 days.
